    "title": "hash: clear HMAC states after use",
    "user": {
      "login": "fametrano",
      "id": 3296421,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTY0MjE=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3296421?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/fametrano",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The RFC6979 initialize and generate functions in `hash_impl.h` never clear their local HMAC states, so the last one stays on the stack after a nonce is derived. It holds an intermediate `V` and an inner digest, not the secret key or the message, and the nonce cannot be recomputed from them without `K`, which the callers clear. `secp256k1_hmac_sha256_clear` exists since #1579 but has no caller.\n\nThis PR clears each state after its last use, and also the SHA256 state that hashes an HMAC key longer than 64 bytes. I added no test. A throwaway program that scans the stack after `secp256k1_nonce_function_rfc6979` finds one copy of `V` before this change and none after, at -O0, -O1 and -O2.\n",
