        "payload": "tree 6f5a7e6e1e0d92056c1c694673e6da46ef6fd36c\nparent 04b91ce295dad7b827ae18eeeed062135a918dae\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792038059 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792038059 +0200\n\nhash: clear HMAC states after use\n\nThe RFC6979 initialize and generate functions keep HMAC states in\nlocal variables and never clear them, so the last state stays on the\nstack after a nonce is derived. secp256k1_hmac_sha256_clear exists for\nthis but has no caller.\n\nClear each of these states after its last use. Also clear the SHA256\nstate that hashes an HMAC key longer than 64 bytes.\n",
